      "message": "Cherry pick is not clean. Checked against UPSTREAM.\nUPSTREAM commit: [googlesource](https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/f4877225313d474659ee53150ccc3d553a978727) [kernel.org](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id\u003df4877225313d474659ee53150ccc3d553a978727).\n\n```\n      ## include/linux/skbuff.h ##\n     @@ include/linux/skbuff.h: typedef unsigned char *sk_buff_data_t;\n    @@ include/linux/skbuff.h: typedef unsigned char *sk_buff_data_t;\n       *\t@sk: Socket we are owned by\n     - *\t@ip_defrag_offset: (aka @sk) alternate use of @sk, used in\n     - *\t\tfragmentation management\n    ++ *\t@android_abi: used to be \u0027ip_defrag_offset\u0027 which was removed in 18685451fc4e\n    ++ *\t              (\"inet: inet_defrag: prevent sk release while still in use\")\n       *\t@dev: Device we arrived on/are leaving by\n       *\t@dev_scratch: (aka @dev) alternate use of @dev when @dev would be %NULL\n       *\t@cb: Control buffer. Free for use by every layer. Put private vars here\n     @@ include/linux/skbuff.h: struct sk_buff {\n    - \t\tstruct llist_node\tll_node;\n    - \t};\n      \n    --\tunion {\n    --\t\tstruct sock\t\t*sk;\n    + \tunion {\n    + \t\tstruct sock\t\t*sk;\n     -\t\tint\t\t\tip_defrag_offset;\n    --\t};\n    -+\tstruct sock\t\t*sk;\n    ++\t\tint\t\t\tandroid_abi; /* Was ip_defrag_offset */\n    + \t};\n      \n      \tunion {\n    - \t\tktime_t\t\ttstamp;\n     \n      ## net/ipv4/inet_fragment.c ##\n     @@\n```\n\n\nPlease refer to the contribution guidelines for details:\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android-mainline/README.md",
